# @tag:system
# @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
#
# Portable smoke for the Trace32 wrapper contract.
#
# The old system spec imported remote debug modules that require Lauterbach
# hardware. This smoke exercises the hardware-free product surface — the
# debugger feature registry the wrapper advertises — so the contract stays
# observable on any host. Live Trace32 protocol/parser coverage belongs in
# focused unit or hardware specs.

# @manual_section: trace32 wrapper portable smoke
"""
## Purpose and audience

Executable evidence that the debugger feature registry backing the Trace32
wrapper exposes its trace32-unique operations and rank constants with the
names and values the debug adapters agree on. For hardware-enablement and
release engineers confirming the t32 lane on hosts without a Lauterbach
probe.

## Operator workflow

Run `./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run
test/03_system/hardware/t32_tools/trace32_wrapper_spec.spl` and confirm
3 examples pass with 0 failures.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the hardware-free registry surface. Nothing here touches a probe
or a t32rem process; adapter connect behavior is out of scope.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

A name or rank mismatch means the feature registry changed — confirm the new
registry value is the agreed wire token, then update the adapter contract
consumers rather than this oracle.
"""
# research: doc/01_research/hardware/t32/trace32_remote_interfaces_2026-03-08.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/hardware/t32_terminal_power_remote.md ; design: doc/05_design/hardware/t32_terminal_power_remote.md

use std.spec.*

use std.spec.step
use std.nogc_sync_mut.debug.remote.feature.features.{FeatureId, FeatureRank}

describe "Trace32 wrapper portable smoke":
    # @manual scenario evidence
    it "exposes the trace32 feature registry names":
        # @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
        # @capture(protocol_json): trace32 feature registry names retained for review
        step("Read the trace32-unique operation names from the product feature registry")
        expect(FeatureId.TraceCapture.to_string()).to_equal("TraceCapture")  # oracle: the registry's wire token for trace capture
        expect(FeatureId.CoverageCollect.to_string()).to_equal("CoverageCollect")  # oracle: the registry's wire token for coverage collection

    it "round-trips the trace capture feature id":
        # @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
        # @capture(protocol_json): id-to-name round trip retained for review
        step("Resolve feature id 40 back to its registry name")
        expect(FeatureId.from_i32(40).to_string()).to_equal("TraceCapture")  # oracle: 40 is the registry id assigned to TraceCapture

    it "reports the native debugger rank":
        # @req REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
        # @capture(statistics): native debugger rank value retained for review
        step("Read the native debugger rank constant from the product registry")
        expect(FeatureRank.NATIVE()).to_equal(0)  # oracle: NATIVE is rank 0 in the debugger feature ranking
